"The shrine was raised about four hundred years ago by a transmigrator of an older wave."
"She came from another world, not Earth, and Fenwatch's tales remember her as the Pale Lady."
"Her name was Isaine, and she held a System legacy of warding that drew on all five elements."
"She found a mouth of the Depths under the fen and sealed it with a wardstone fed by five elements."
"She built the shrine over the wardstone and died there, spent, as the seal closed."
"Her bones lie in the flooded undercroft beside the wardstone, still holding unspent integration."
"Those remains drew the System's weave to the Greyfen when it made Nala's body."
"The undercroft holds the wardstone, her bones, her slate journals in her own script, and her staff."
"The wardstone is a waist-high pillar of pale crystal, now nearly dark, with five sockets in it."
"Over four centuries the fen's settling tilted the shrine and cracked the undercroft."
"Fed with all five elements, the wardstone would wake and close the Sink again."
"Nala's reserves hold all five elements and could feed the wardstone, at a heavy draw."
"Isaine's journals tell how she made the seal, and how the Depths below it are shaped."
"Her staff of pale wood carries a trace of her warding and answers to anyone holding five elements."
